{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1314","id":5007152955,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABKnMXOw","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1314","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1314.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1314.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1314","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1314/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1314/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1314/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/1a5a5acb9323879fae5d16a9724855abff7d67b9","number":1314,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"T-3108: 1801 Prairie's south-west corner as a round bay, from HABS photograph 1","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## T-3108 — 1801 Prairie's south-west corner from HABS photograph 1\n\n**What a visitor sees:** the W. W. Kimball house at 1801 Prairie now turns its front's south-west corner in a **two-storey round bay**, with one window a storey under a pierced stone balcony, as Harold Allen's June 1965 HABS photograph shows it. Before this, the gabled pavilion ran flat to a 0.44 m chamfer. The pavilion beside the round is narrower now, with its paired windows and carved gable centred on its face.\n\n### What changed\n- **Kit (additive):** a K08 bay may now stand `on_chamfer` of a chamfered projection. Its wall is the cant, `s_m` is measured along it, and on the host wall it reaches over the cant's span (`k01_frontage_params._bays`, `k01_frontage.bay`). A chamfer that a round bay stands on may run up to 2.0 m along the front (at most half the pavilion's width) and 1.6 m behind it. A bare chamfer keeps T-3048's 1.0 m / 0.6 m limits (`CHAMFER_ALONG_M` now sits beside `CHAMFER_BEHIND_M`).\n- **Record:** p_south's chamfer is now 1.3 m along by 1.4 m behind; the 1911 sheet cuts the corner back about 1.0–1.4 m. The face is now 2.85 m (v 6.85–9.7) and its pairs 1.5 m clear (they were 2.0 m). The gable now spans the whole face (inset dropped), with pitch 2.49 so the apex keeps T-3015's Taylor-matched height. `sw_round` is a bow on the cut: chord 1.684 m, rise 0.5 m, storeys 5.0 + 3.7 m to 8.7 m under the moulded stone cornice, one transomed sash a storey, and the front bow's pierced lattice balustrade in two panels. The south wall's downpipe by the front corner was removed: the cut takes the corner, and HABS 1 shows no pipe there.\n- **HABS 1's camera is re-solved** on the rebuilt corner. Focal length, principal point and roll were held; eye and heading were fitted to the pavilion's edges and rows, the round and the SE cornice (rms 11.8 px). **The old 85 px cornice gap, re-measured:** the round's wall top now renders ~19 px under the print's, its balustrade rail ~50 px under, and the SE cornice ~23 px over.\n- **Match records re-read, both still `differs`.**\n  - HABS: corner bay **fixed**; face width within tolerance (~20 px, ~0.3 m).\n  - Still **open**: cornice/rail heights; the small light over the balcony, which is not built (K08's sash on the cant rendered with its recess occluded, so I took it out); and the loggia end of the front, where the arch renders ~117 px north of the print's through the corner-fitted camera. The front's layout north of the pavilion and this picture don't agree.\n  - Within tolerance: the gable's height, where the two photographs disagree (HABS puts the finial ~1.2 m lower than the Taylor print does) and the build keeps the period print's.\n  - Taylor: the face renders x 1227–1325 against the print's 1230–1332 (before this change: 109 px against 105); the round's cornice and balustrade show just past the face, as the print's cornice does.\n- **Liberty** `L-kimball-1801-round-bay-3108` records the reconstructed sizes and the face-width compromise (sheet 2.4 m, photographs 3.4–3.7 m, built 2.85 m).\n- **Tests follow the record:** `test_k01_pavilion_past_eave` (new chamfer values, `on_chamfer` refusals, bare-chamfer limits still enforced); `test_k08_gable` (T-3073's inset is now held on a copy); `check_bay_kit`'s chamfer key.\n- The other K01/K12/K13/K16 meshes were re-emitted after the generator edit and are byte-identical.\n\nT-3109 (south face and roof), T-3110 (east and rear) and the full T-1890 stay open.\n\n### Verification\n- `tools/check.sh` in two passes, because the full gate takes longer than the 600 s foreground cap here. Each pass skipped the other's step labels and both ran to their own summary. **Pass A: CHECK PASS, 508 steps, none red.** **Pass B: 537 of 538 green.** The red step was \"Source-use backlinks\" (the coverage page's liberty count went 766 → 767); I rebuilt the page with `compile_source_use.py` and `--check` now passes. `validate.py --stale` is clean.\n- Smoke `--published`: desktop part 3 **107 passed, 0 failed** (5 m 21 s); mobile part 3 **107 passed, 0 failed**, run twice, the second on the final merged tree (2 m 25 s). Zero page errors.\n- Not re-run on the final head: desktop part 3, which last ran before the dev merge and the 0.384 → 0.5 m rise. The hosted gate covers the head.\n- Side-by-sides: `docs/RESEARCH/photo-match/kimball_house_1801_prairie/`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T17:49:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T20:36:54Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T20:36:44Z","merged_at":"2026-10-25T20:36:44Z","merge_commit_sha":"ee9fc81107f561f38e728f938d38a641fa484405","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/t3108-kimball-round-corner-bay","ref":"steward/t3108-kimball-round-corner-bay","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description"